   ideas:["Solids: particles touching in rows, vibrating; fixed shape and volume.","Liquids: particles touching but randomly arranged, sliding past each other; flow and take the container's shape.","Gases: particles far apart, moving fast in all directions; fill their container and can be squashed.","Changes of state: melting, freezing, boiling/evaporating, condensing, sublimation. Mass stays the same; particles don't change, only their arrangement and energy.","Heating gives particles more energy. Melting point and boiling point are fixed for a pure substance (water: 0 °C and 100 °C)."],
